# Workflow

## Gherkin First
Every feature must have a Gherkin scenario written in `docs/features/` before any code is written.

```gherkin
Feature: [Feature name]
  Scenario: [What the user does]
    Given [starting state]
    When [action taken]
    Then [expected result]
```

If the user asks to build something without a Gherkin scenario, ask them to write one first.

## One Feature at a Time
- Build exactly what the current Gherkin scenario describes — nothing more
- Do not add features, improvements, or "nice to haves" that aren't in the spec
- When a feature is complete and tested against its Gherkin, commit before starting the next

## Commits
Use conventional commit format:
```
feat: add generate social post endpoint
fix: brand context not saving on update
chore: add supabase migration for outputs table
```

## Scope Discipline
If a new idea comes up mid-feature, stop. Do not build it. Note it for later. Finish the current feature first.
